\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Governor of Illinois Creates New  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights Group\b0\par\par\uc2 By Maggie Astor \par \uc2 477 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 October 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 19\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mr. Pritzker's organization, Think Big America, will support ballot measures to codify or restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, seeking to elevate an issue that has energized Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 J.B. Pritzker\uc2  of Illinois is starting an advocacy group to promote \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights around the country, seeking to blunt the impact of the Supreme Court's decision overturning Roe v. Wade and to elevate an issue that has energized Democrats in elections.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Pritzker, who easily won re-election last year, has not said how much of his own money he will invest in the new organization, but he is worth billions of dollars. The new organization, Think Big America, will help fund state ballot measures -- typically expensive endeavors -- to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in states whose legislatures have enacted or could enact \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Voters have consistently supported such measures since the court did away with the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, approving them in every state where they have been offered and, conversely, rejecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in every state where they have been proposed.\par \par \uc2 One such measure will be on the ballot in Ohio next month: a constitutional amendment that would establish a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , contraception, fertility treatment and miscarriage care. Ohio has a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on the books that is not currently in effect because of a legal challenge, but that could take effect if the state Supreme Court allows it.\par \par \uc2 Efforts are underway to have similar measures on ballots in Arizona, Florida and Nevada next year.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Think Big America said the group was providing ''financial and strategic support'' to the campaigns in Ohio, Arizona and Nevada, including putting members on advisory boards, helping to develop messaging and analyzing polls. She added that it was also prepared to help with direct voter contact and, if applicable, legal challenges.\par \par \uc2 The creation of the organization was first reported by The 19th and The Chicago Sun-Times.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Pritzker is widely seen as a future presidential candidate, and -- like another possible White House contender, Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  of California -- has advertised his state as an oasis from Republican policies and an emblem of Democratic governance.\par \par \uc2 In a video on Wednesday, Mr. Pritzker condemned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, but also singled out Republican efforts to restrict voting and to ban some books discussing race and gender from school curriculums and libraries -- suggesting that his organization could eventually focus on those issues, too.\par \par \uc2 ''Over the last few years, the far-right agenda has only become more extreme,'' he said. ''The end of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , widespread book bans, a rollback of voting rights and civil rights, the erosion of trust in our institutions -- that will be our permanent reality if we don't act now.''\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page A19. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020231019ejaj0004i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
