\par\par \uc2 Movies, Performing Arts/Weekend Desk; SECTC\par \b \uc2 Plan C\b0\par\par\uc2 By Teo Bugbee \par \uc2 390 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 October 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 In this documentary by Tracy Droz Tragos, each of the film's subjects considers how far past the line of legal comfort they can afford to cross.\par \par \uc2 The director Tracy Droz Tragos anchors her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  documentary ''Plan C'' on a grass-roots organization by the same name. At the center of the organization is Francine Coeytaux, a public health activist in the United States, previously known for her campaign to get contraceptive pills sold over the counter at pharmacies.\par \par \uc2 Under the leadership of Coeytaux and Elisa Wells, the group, which was founded in 2015, focuses on providing information to patients about medical suppliers and providers who can prescribe at-home \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills -- medication which can safely end a pregnancy up to 12 weeks.\par \par \uc2 The footage of Plan C's activities covers four years, beginning in 2019 and extending after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade in 2022. Some scenes of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers at work are shot v\u233\'00\'E9rit\u233\'00\'E9 style, while in others Coeytaux and her associates speak directly to the camera about their efforts to assist people seeking abortions.\par \par \uc2 Plan C's methods are mobile, often including telehealth or prescriptions delivered by mail, and the group's actions come with both legal and physical risks.\par \par \uc2 [Video: Watch on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 .]\par \par \uc2 There are over a dozen doctors, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates and patients interviewed in this film, and most don't reveal their full names for safety reasons, fearing violence from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists or prosecution in states such as Texas, where residents can receive rewards for reporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. Some don't reveal their faces, and Tragos blurs their images or conceals identifying features.\par \par \uc2 At times, all of the secrecy and legal caution can make it hard to understand the complex logistics of getting a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the United States. But the risks involved are bracingly apparent, and the documentary benefits from its attempts to capture Plan C's high-stakes operation in progress.\par \par \uc2 As people navigate this new reality, each of the film's subjects considers how far past the line of legal comfort they can afford to cross.\par \par \uc2 Plan C\par \par \uc2 Not rated. Running time: 1 hour 39 minutes. In theaters.\par \par \uc2 Not rated. Running time: 1 hour 39 minutes. In theaters.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page C6. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020231013ejad0003h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
