\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Democrat's Ad for State Post Points to  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  and Jan. 6\b0\par\par\uc2 By Trip Gabriel \par \uc2 617 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 September 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 16\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ryan Bizzarro, a Democrat and member of Pennsylvania's House of Representatives, announced a bid to challenge the Republican incumbent, Stacy Garrity, by invoking issues galvanizing to Democrats.\par \par \uc2 A Pennsylvania Democrat announced a bid for state treasurer on Tuesday by seeking to tie his Republican opponent to two of the country's most incendiary issues: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and the Jan. 6, 2021, attack on the U.S. Capitol.\par \par \uc2 In his announcement video, Ryan Bizzarro, a member of the state House of Representatives, accuses the Republican incumbent, Stacy Garrity, of being ''Pennsylvania's highest-ranking extremist office holder.'' He highlights her past support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and her appearance at a rally in Harrisburg the day before the Capitol riot in which she appeared to endorse former President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 's false claims that the election was rigged.\par \par \uc2 Campaigns for a lower-profile office like state treasurer -- where the duties include managing the government's cash flow, not setting policy -- have tended to fly under voters' radars. But in a battleground state like Pennsylvania, where the presidency and a \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  seat will be fiercely contested in 2024, down-ballot races, too, can take on intense partisanship over issues with little connection to an official's duties.\par \par \uc2 ''She's one of those extreme folks we've got to get rid of,'' Mr. Bizzarro said in an interview. His opening salvo takes a page from the playbook of Gov. \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , a Democrat who ran in 2022 against a hard-right opponent by promising to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and voting rights. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in particular proved a galvanizing issue for Democrats in the midterm elections after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade. But while Pennsylvania's governor has immense sway over those issues, its treasurer does not.\par \par \uc2 A campaign adviser to Ms. Garrity, Dennis Roddy, said that bringing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Jan. 6 into the race was an effort to dodge the fact that Ms. Garrity has been a successful steward of Pennsylvania's money.\par \par \uc2 ''She's done a hell of a job, she's well liked and this is just the usual 'let's nationalize an election we can't win on the merits,''' he said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Bizzarro's announcement video begins with harrowing scenes of the violent attack on the Capitol, then cuts to Ms. Garrity at a Jan. 5, 2021, rally in Harrisburg that was organized to pressure Pennsylvania lawmakers to decertify the state's vote for \uc2 Joseph R. Biden Jr\uc2 . After courts in Pennsylvania had already rejected multiple claims of fraud by the Trump campaign and allies, Ms. Garrity insisted to the crowd, ''The election from this November is tarnished forever.''\par \par \uc2 Ms. Garrity, an Iraq war veteran who defeated a Democratic incumbent in 2020, has also shown an inclination to lean into national issues. Her campaign \uc2 Facebook\uc2  page recently criticized Mr. Biden's ''hasty and spineless retreat'' from Afghanistan, equated ''Bidenomics=Bideninflation'' and joined a chorus of Republican critics of Senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 's shorts-and-sweatshirt wardrobe.\par \par \uc2 In the past, Ms. Garrity, 59, has asked people to ''please pray'' for the Supreme Court to reverse Roe v. Wade and called to defund \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 . In 2020, she boasted of being endorsed by Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, a group that says it exists ''to end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Bizzarro, 37, the House Democratic Policy Chair, comes from a family of professional prizefighters in Erie County, Pa. It is unclear if he will have a primary competitor. He appears in his video inside a boxing ring.\par \par \uc2 Ryan Bizzarro This article appeared in print on page A16. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020230927ej9r0004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
