\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Kennedy Backtracks On Backing  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban\b0\par\par\uc2 By Maggie Astor \par \uc2 551 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 August 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 19\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mr. Kennedy, who is running for president as a Democrat, said that he would sign a ban after three months' gestation, but his campaign quickly reversed his comments.\par \par \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr. said Sunday that he supported a federal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the first trimester of pregnancy, then quickly backtracked -- underscoring both his ideologically uncomfortable position within the Democratic primary field and the deep salience of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in next year's election.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kennedy, who is running against President Biden, made his comments at the Iowa State Fair after an NBC News reporter asked whether he would sign a bill codifying the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once protected by Roe v. Wade. Democrats have rallied around such legislation since the Supreme Court overturned Roe last year, though the party does not currently have the votes in Congress to pass it.\par \par \uc2 ''I believe a decision to abort a child should be up to the woman during the first three months of life,'' Mr. Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 In response to follow-up questions, Mr. Kennedy confirmed that he would sign federal restrictions after three months, which some Republicans have proposed and elected Democrats almost universally oppose. While the vast majority of abortions take place in that first-trimester window, Roe protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights until viability -- the point when a fetus can survive outside the womb -- which is around the end of the second trimester.\par \par \uc2 Hours later, Mr. Kennedy's campaign released a statement saying he had ''misunderstood a question posed to him by an NBC reporter in a crowded, noisy exhibit hall at the Iowa State Fair.''\par \par \uc2 ''Mr. Kennedy's position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is that it is always the woman's right to choose,'' the statement said. ''He does not support legislation banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .''\par \par \uc2 But the video of his comments and the back-and-forth that followed show Mr. Kennedy specifying the first three months of pregnancy in his own words, and the reporter asking several follow-up questions to confirm his position.\par \par \uc2 ''So you would cap it at 15 weeks?'' the reporter asked.\par \par \uc2 ''Yes,'' Mr. Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 ''Or 21 weeks?''\par \par \uc2 ''Yes, three months,'' he said.\par \par \uc2 ''So three months, you would sign a federal cap on that,'' the reporter said.\par \par \uc2 ''Yes, I would,'' Mr. Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for his campaign did not respond to questions on Monday.\par \par \uc2 While there was no ambiguity in Mr. Kennedy's declaration of support for a ban after three months, there were indications that he did not understand the timeline of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 By way of explaining his position, he said, ''Once a child is viable outside the womb, I think then the state has an interest in protecting that child.'' But viability, which can vary from pregnancy to pregnancy, is generally around 24 weeks, or six months.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kennedy, a scion of the storied American political family and an environmental lawyer, has become known for his anti-vaccine advocacy and his promotion of conspiracy theories. While he is running for president as a Democrat, some of his positions are more in line with Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Some of the positions Robert F. Kennedy Jr. holds are more in line with Republicans. (PHOTOGRAPH BY JORDAN GALE FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) This article appeared in print on page A19. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020230815ej8f0004g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
