\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 An Iowa Ban On Abortions After 6 Weeks Becomes Law\b0\par\par\uc2 By Colbi Edmonds \par \uc2 764 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 12\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The News\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  of Iowa, a Republican, signed a strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban into law on Friday, even as a judge heard arguments to suspend it.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Reynolds had vowed to sign the measure that was passed this week by the Legislature. It was immediately challenged in Polk County court by the American Civil Liberties Union and Planned Parenthood, and on Friday those groups were in court seeking to temporarily block the law while their legal case moved forward.\par \par \uc2 The new law bans most abortions after cardiac activity is detected, which anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups say is around six weeks of pregnancy, before most women know they are pregnant. It takes effect immediately, and dramatically changes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state.\par \par \uc2 ''As we gather here today -- and at this very moment -- the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry is in court trying to prevent this law from taking effect and stop the will of the people once again,'' Ms. Reynolds said at the signing.\par \par \uc2 Pam Jochum, the Democratic leader of the Iowa Senate, called the law a ''dangerous attack on Iowa women'' on Friday and said that she looked forward to ''Iowa courts blocking this law.''\par \par \uc2 Why It Matters\par \par \uc2 The change now adds Iowa to a list of Republican-led states that have moved to ban or severely restrict the procedure since the Supreme Court eliminated the national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, sending the matter back to the states to set policy.\par \par \uc2 The ban also shuts off another area of access for women in the region, as nearby states including Wisconsin, North Dakota and South Dakota also have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 More than a dozen states now have bans that prohibit most abortions after conception or very early in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Background\par \par \uc2 After the state's previous six-week ban was blocked when a deadlocked Iowa Supreme Court left it unenforceable, Governor Reynolds called a special session on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers returned to the State Capitol and passed a nearly identical set of restrictions on the procedure. Iowa providers and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates filed suit on Wednesday within hours of the Legislature's passage, saying it was unconstitutional under the standard of ''undue burden.''\par \par \uc2 The session further cemented Iowa's sharp political shift to the right, and ended its increasingly rare status as a Republican-led state where abortions are allowed up to 20 weeks post-fertilization, or roughly 22 weeks into pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The bill passed by Republicans allows for abortions until the point where there is what the bill calls ''detectable fetal heartbeat,'' a term that medical groups dispute.\par \par \uc2 The legislation assumes this is roughly six weeks of pregnancy. The legislation includes exceptions after that point in cases of rape or incest, when the woman's life is in serious danger or she faces a risk of certain permanent injuries, or when fetal abnormalities ''incompatible with life'' are present.\par \par \uc2 What's Next\par \par \uc2 If \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists prevail in court, the law could be suspended at least temporarily while the legal case proceeds.\par \par \uc2 Joseph Seidlin, a district court judge in Polk County, said he would not make a ruling on Friday, even as the groups pushing for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights said the law would lead to immediate harms.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Seidlin said the decision required ''strong and lengthy attention,'' and making an immediate ruling from the bench would be perceived as a flippant decision.\par \par \uc2 ''I cannot think of anything that would be more insulting to either side,'' he said.\par \par \uc2 Peter Im, staff attorney at the \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2 , had requested that the ruling be made from the bench because of the ban's ''devastating impacts for Iowans'' and argued that the ban was a violation of state constitutional rights.\par \par \uc2 ''If there's any wisdom to be gleaned from our nation's experience during this past year, I think that it's when there's an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in place, people suffer,'' Mr. Im said.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Johnston, assistant attorney general in Iowa, said that under the ''rational basis'' test -- used to determine whether the state has a legitimate interest in a law -- the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law was constitutional.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Johnston represents Governor Reynolds, the State of Iowa and the \uc2 Iowa Board of Medicine\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He said that the plaintiffs failed to consider the loss of ''unborn life'' as a result of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that the new law ''aims to prevent the destruction of human lives.''\par \par \uc2 Kate Zernike and Mitch Smith contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 Kate Zernike and Mitch Smith contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page A12. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020230715ej7f0003c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
