\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Using Pills May Be Safe After 12 Weeks\b0\par\par\uc2 By Roni Caryn Rabin \par \uc2 686 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 July 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 11\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The News\par \par \uc2 An overwhelming majority of women were able to end unwanted pregnancies with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medications on their own and without additional medical procedures, even if they were well beyond the first trimester, according to a report published on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The study was based on the experiences of 264 women who were nine to 16 weeks pregnant in Argentina, Nigeria and an unnamed country in Southeast Asia where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal. Almost half of the women took only one drug, misoprostol, instead of the standard two-drug regimen, mifepristone and misoprostol.\par \par \uc2 They were nonetheless able to terminate the pregnancies, according to the study, published in the journal Obstetrics & Gynecology. All of the participants received information from an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  support group.\par \par \uc2 The findings align with clinical data showing the efficacy and safety of medication abortions conducted under medical supervision throughout pregnancy, said Ruvani Jayaweera, an epidemiologist and research scientist at Ibis \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Health\b0 \highlight\uc2  and one of the study's authors.\par \par \uc2 Nearly one in four women sought medical care after the abortions, most frequently to confirm that the termination was complete. A smaller percentage wanted to address concerns about bleeding, pain, fever or discharge.\par \par \uc2 Women who were pregnant for 12 weeks or longer were significantly more likely to seek medical care after a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , compared with those who were nine to 11 weeks pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Why It Matters\par \par \uc2 As more than a dozen states banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past year, women with unwanted pregnancies have turned in growing numbers to self-managed medication abortions.\par \par \uc2 But the arduous and time-consuming methods needed to procure the drugs create delays, often meaning pregnancies are more advanced by the time the drugs arrive. The new study, one of the first to report on self-managed medication abortions carried out after the first trimester of pregnancy, offers these women some reassurance, researchers said.\par \par \uc2 ''This paper adds to previous research indicating that self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with medications is safe and effective, including after 12 weeks of pregnancy,'' said Dr. \uc2 Daniel Grossman\uc2 , a professor of obstetrics, gynecology and reproductive sciences at the \uc2 University of California, San Francisco\uc2 . ''As clinic-based \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care becomes less available in many parts of the country due to state-level bans, self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will become more common, as we are already seeing.''\par \par \uc2 The research also suggests an alternative path to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if access to mifepristone is severely curtailed. In April, the Supreme Court blocked a lower-court ruling that would have stopped the distribution and sale of mifepristone throughout the United States while the case wends its way through the legal system.\par \par \uc2 Some 44 percent of the participants in the new study used only misoprostol, which is prescribed for many conditions and available in many countries without a prescription.\par \par \uc2 Background\par \par \uc2 About 90 percent of the women in the study succeeded at ending pregnancies with self-managed medication abortions, without any additional intervention needed. Five percent had a procedure to complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and 5 percent had an incomplete \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The two-drug regimen of mifepristone and misoprostol is approved by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  for use through only 10 weeks of pregnancy, under the supervision of a health care provider.\par \par \uc2 But the W.H.O., taking into account shortages of health care providers in much of the developing world, endorses self-managed medical abortions in pregnancies of up to 12 weeks without medical supervision.\par \par \uc2 What's Next\par \par \uc2 The new report was a sub-analysis of a larger study that looked at 1,352 women who self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at different stages of pregnancy, and the number with more advanced gestations was relatively small.\par \par \uc2 Only three participants self-managed abortions with gestations of 17 weeks and longer, and the study's authors called for more research into medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and later pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Access to drugs that are used for these abortions, which are often ordered through the mail, continues to be a flashpoint in the ongoing debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the United States.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page A11. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020230707ej770003f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
