\par\par \uc2 POLITICAL MEMO\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 G.O.P. Finds It Hard to Tie Biden to Culture Wars\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reid J. Epstein \par \uc2 1,502 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 July 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Despite his alliance with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters and L.G.B.T.Q. advocates, the president has deftly avoided becoming enmeshed in battles over hotly contested social issues.\par \par \uc2 President Biden memorably jumped the gun on Barack Obama in endorsing same-sex marriage more than a decade ago, but at a June fund-raiser near San Francisco, he couldn't recall the letters L.G.B.T.Q.\par \par \uc2 And even as the Democratic Party makes the fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights central to its political message, Mr. Biden last week declared himself ''not big on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .''\par \par \uc2 At a moment when the American political parties are trading fierce fire from the trenches of a war over social and cultural policy, the president is staying out of the fray.\par \par \uc2 White, male, 80 years old and not particularly up-to-date on the language of the left, Mr. Biden has largely avoided becoming enmeshed in contemporary battles over gender, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other hotly contested social issues -- even as he does things like hosting what he called ''the largest Pride Month celebration ever held at the White House.''\par \par \uc2 Republicans have tried to pull him in, but appear to recognize the difficulty: When G.O.P. presidential candidates vow to end what they derisively call ''woke'' culture, they often aim their barbs not directly at Mr. Biden but at big corporations like \uc2 Disney\uc2  and BlackRock or the vast ''administrative state'' of the federal government. Republican strategists say most of their party's message on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and transgender issues is aimed at primary voters, while Mr. Biden is seen as far more vulnerable in a general election on the economy, crime and immigration.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's armor against cultural attacks might seem unlikely for a president who has strongly advocated for L.G.B.T.Q. people, the leader of a party whose fortunes ride on the wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics, and a man who owes his presidency to unbending support from Black Democratic primary voters.\par \par \uc2 Yet despite adopting positions over the years that pushed Democrats -- and then the country -- to embrace more liberal attitudes on social issues, Mr. Biden has kept himself at arm's length from elements of his party that could pose him political problems. In June, the White House said it had barred a transgender activist who went topless at its Pride event.\par \par \uc2 And while Mr. Biden's age has become one of his chief political weaknesses, both his allies and adversaries say it also helps insulate him from cultural attacks by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 ''Everybody wants to talk about how old \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is, but the truth of the matter is it's his age and his experience that allow him to be who he is and allow him to say the things and to help people in a way that nobody else can,'' said Henry R. Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz III, a former \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  finance director. Mr. Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz, who is gay, had Mr. Biden serve as his wedding officiant in 2017.\par \par \uc2 Much of Mr. Biden's loyalty from L.G.B.T.Q. Democrats stems from his 2012 endorsement of same-sex marriages when Mr. Obama was still officially opposed to them. Mr. Biden's position was seen as politically risky at the time, before the Supreme Court in 2015 recognized the right of same-sex couples to marry, but has evolved into something he bragged about during his 2020 campaign.\par \par \uc2 He has also been on the forefront of recognizing transgender rights. In his first week in office, Mr. Biden ended the Trump-era ban on transgender troops in the military. In December, he signed into law federal protections for same-sex marriages.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, Mr. Biden has not adopted the terminology of progressive activists or allowed himself to be drawn into public debates that might leave him outside the political mainstream. On Thursday, after the Supreme Court's major ruling ending affirmative action in college admissions, a reporter asked him, ''Is this a rogue court?''\par \par \uc2 Pausing to think for a moment, Mr. Biden responded, ''This is not a normal court.''\par \par \uc2 He also does not always remember the words most American politicians use to describe L.G.B.T.Q. people. At the fund-raiser near San Francisco last month, Mr. Biden lamented the Supreme Court's decision last year that ended the national right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and suggested the court was coming for gay rights next.\par \par \uc2 Paraphrasing two of the conservative justices, he said: ''There's no constitutional right in the law for H-B, excuse me, for gay, lesbian, you know, the whole, the whole group. There's no constitutional protection.''\par \par \uc2 During a stop at the Iowa State Fair during his 2020 campaign, a conservative provocateur trailing the Democratic presidential candidates asked Mr. Biden, ''How many genders are there?''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden replied: ''There are at least three. Don't play games with me, kid.''\par \par \uc2 Then, perhaps not realizing that his inquisitor was a right-wing activist, Mr. Biden added: ''By the way, first one to come out for marriage was me.''\par \par \uc2 Sarah McBride, a Delaware state senator who recently began a campaign to become the first transgender member of Congress, said Mr. Biden's language gave him the ability to solidify Democrats behind a progressive social agenda and ''reach communities and demographics that are not yet fully in the coalition.''\par \par \uc2 ''He's not getting caught up on rhetoric that isn't understandable for your middle-of-the-road voter,'' Ms. McBride said.\par \par \uc2 She also pointed to Mr. Biden's age as helpful for making Democrats' case on social issues without alienating skeptical voters.\par \par \uc2 ''His background allows him to say things that I think would be heard as more radical if they were said by a younger politician,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 As majorities of Americans have accepted gay marriage, social conservatives have made opposition to transgender rights a mainstay of their politics. And Republicans running to displace Mr. Biden have tended to focus on energizing G.O.P. primary voters rather than making a villain out of the president.\par \par \uc2 ''It's hard to paint an 80-year-old white man as a flaming woke warrior,'' said \uc2 Whit Ayres\uc2 , a longtime pollster for Republican candidates.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of Florida is perhaps the leading purveyor of Republicans' anti-''woke'' message, throwing barbs both online and in speeches. On Friday, his campaign cast even Mr. Trump as too liberal on L.G.B.T.Q. issues in a provocative video posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At a June rally in Tulsa, Okla., Mr. DeSantis described being approached by military veterans who don't want their children and grandchildren joining the armed forces because of liberal policy changes instituted by Democrats -- though the governor blamed Mr. Obama as much as he did Mr. Biden.\par \par \uc2 ''A woke military is not going to be a strong military,'' Mr. DeSantis said. ''You got to get the politicization out of it. And on Day 1, we're ripping out all the Obama-Biden policies to woke-ify the military.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden has never presented as a left-wing culture warrior. A Catholic, he has long been wary about jumping headlong into fights over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Even as his campaign and party are preparing to make his re-election bid a referendum on Republican efforts to further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. Biden proclaimed to a crowd of donors in suburban Washington that he himself was not eager to do so.\par \par \uc2 ''You know, I happen to be a practicing Catholic,'' Mr. Biden said last week. ''I'm not big on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But guess what? Roe v. Wade got it right.''\par \par \uc2 That stance has long caused some consternation among Democrats. It took until June 2019, weeks after beginning his 2020 campaign and under immense pressure from allies in his party, for Mr. Biden to renounce his long-held support for banning federal funding for abortions.\par \par \uc2 Renee Bracey Sherman, the founder of We Testify, a group that shares women's stories of having abortions, said Mr. Biden would need to adopt a more forceful position in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to energize liberal voters in 2024. She suggested that in the same way Mr. Biden hosts championship sports teams at the White House, he should invite women who have had abortions to come and tell their stories.\par \par \uc2 ''The midterms show that Americans love \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,'' Ms. Bracey Sherman said. ''\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a higher approval rating than he does. He should be riding the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wave.''\par \par \uc2 Kristi Eaton contributed reporting from Tulsa, Okla.\par \par \uc2 Kristi Eaton contributed reporting from Tulsa, Okla.\par \par \uc2 President Biden at a Pride celebration on the south lawn of the White House last month. At left, L.G.B.T.Q. protesters outside the annual Moms for Liberty summit in Philadelphia last week. (PHOTOGRAPHS BY PETE MAROVICH FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES; HAIYUN JIANG FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) (A12) This article appeared in print on page A1, A12. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020230705ej750003z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
